&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;L&#39;équipe Data Platform de DECATHLON recherche ses futur-e-s Développeur-se-s Full Stack basé·e·s à Lille/Paris.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Au cœur de l’entité Decathlon Digital, nous recherchons nos futur.es Développeur·se·s&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Full Stack &lt;/strong&gt;pour rejoindre les équipes Data Factory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cette plateforme technologique, globale à tout le groupe de manière internationale, soutient le développement de l’usage de la Data chez Decathlon, du calcul du chiffre d’affaires à l’aide de conception de produits innovants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nous opérons une Modern Data Stack de pointe, avec un Lakehouse comme centre de gravité. Notre mission ? Garantir la scalabilité, l&#39;automatisation et l&#39;excellence des pratiques de développement pour l&#39;ensemble de nos communautés (Data Engineers, Analysts, Scientists).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ton futur terrain de jeu&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;La Data Factory est organisée en équipes expertes, chacune pilotée par un binôme Tech Lead &amp;amp; Product Manager. Selon ton profil et tes affinités, tu intégreras l’un de nos collectifs :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎨 Équipe UserXP (User Experience)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tu es l&#39;interface entre la plateforme et ses utilisateurs. Ton rôle est de concevoir des outils et des workflows qui simplifient la vie des développeurs data, en mettant l&#39;accent sur l&#39;ergonomie et l&#39;efficacité opérationnelle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📥 Équipe Ingestion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ton objectif : rendre l&#39;ingestion de données &quot;seamless&quot;. Tu développes et maintiens nos solutions internes (DFI - Data Factory Ingestion) pour garantir un flux de données fluide, normé et automatisé vers le datalake.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;STACK TECHNIQUE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un environnement full cloud (AWS-GCP)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kubernetes, avec full CI/CD (Flux, Github Action...)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;S3, Redshift, PostgreSQL, GCS, BigQuery&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EMR, Databricks, AWS Athena&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Airflow&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Jira/Confluence, GitHub&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Langages : (au moins 2 parmi) : Python, Java, JavaScript/TypeScript&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frameworks/Librairies : React, Angular, Vue.js, Spring, Django, Flask, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TA FUTURE CONTRIBUTION&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tu seras en charge de:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concevoir, développer et maintenir des composants front-end et back-end de la plateforme data, en mettant l&#39;accent sur l&#39;expérience développeur et l&#39;automatisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribuer à la mise en place d&#39;une plateforme data self-service, en fournissant des outils et des services qui simplifient le développement, le déploiement et l&#39;exploitation des solutions data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Développer des API et des services robustes et évolutifs pour l&#39;accès et la manipulation des données.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implémenter des interfaces utilisateur intuitives pour les outils et services de la plateforme data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automatiser les processus de développement, de test et de déploiement (CI/CD) pour garantir une livraison rapide et fiable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborer étroitement avec les équipes Data Science, Data Engineering et Ops pour comprendre leurs besoins et y répondre efficacement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participer à la veille technologique et proposer des solutions innovantes pour améliorer la plateforme data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apprendre et appliquer les bonnes pratiques de développement logiciel, de test et de documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DECATHLON DIGITAL&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Imaginez si la technologie nous permettait de repousser les frontières et d&#39;offrir des expériences sportives inédites. C&#39;est précisément notre ambition chez Decathlon Digital ! Nous sommes une équipe de plus de 5 000 experts en ingénierie logicielle, gestion de produits, données, cloud et cybersécurité, répartis à Paris, Lille et Amsterdam. Ensemble, nous créons la plus vaste plateforme sportive numérique, en exploitant les innovations technologiques pour optimiser la chaîne de valeur, concevoir des expériences connectées et donner une seconde vie à nos produits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Changeons la donne pour de bon.&lt;/strong&gt; Notre passion du sport nous guide et nous voulons qu’elle perdure. C’est pourquoi nous nous engageons à bâtir un modèle technologique plus durable, en réduisant notre impact direct sur l&#39;environnement, et en créant un espace sûr et inclusif pour apprendre et nous épanouir ensemble. Rejoins l’équipe et façonnons le futur du sport.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Oxford, England&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; As needed&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Job ID:&lt;/strong&gt; 1905&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Technical Programme Manager to join the Quantum Systems Infrastructure (QSI) team at IonQ&#39;s Oxford office. QSI builds and runs the platform our next-generation quantum computers are built, tested, released and operated on, from bare metal in the lab to cloud, working across both Oxford and the US.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your mission is to run the machinery that keeps QSI’s portfolio visible, planned and unblocked so engineers can engineer, leaders can lead, and the business always knows what is changing and why it matters. You will work very closely with the Technical Programme Managers in the Software and Science teams, ensuring our processes and workflows complement and integrate with their work, rather than duplicating effort.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We run a centralised PMO operating model at IonQ which you will be a core part of though on a day to day basis you will work alongside the QSI team. As part of this model, this role will not make technical decisions, own engineering headcount, or define product but it will make the programme around those things run.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own programme execution across QSI’s delivery streams, translating a leadership-visible roadmap into clear plans, measurable milestones and predictable delivery. You will create and run the operating rhythm that keeps teams aligned and leaders informed. When priorities shift, you will implement structure to that ambiguity, clarifying scope, coordinating trade-offs and pushing problems to resolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning programme execution across QSI’s delivery streams: one planning rhythm, one backlog discipline, ensuring dependencies and risks surfaced early and chased to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Running the roadmap-to-delivery link: keeping the roadmap, Jira and reality agreeing with each other, and making slippage visible early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the programme ceremonies and the design of the workflows behind them (day-to-day stand-ups are run by the engineering managers).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working hand-in-hand with the Software and Science TPMs: shared or integrated processes wherever teams interact, and no duplicated ceremonies, boards or reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinating across teams - Continuing Engineering (US), the PMO, product and science teams - serving as QSI’s cross-functional programme liaison.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establishing programme cadences and reporting (changelogs, demos, leadership summaries etc) in plain English that non-infrastructure stakeholders can read and trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Running the intake and triage process so requests reach the right stream with the right priority, without engineers being interrupt-driven.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a technically fluent Programme Manager who brings structure, pace and clarity to a fast-moving infrastructure organisation. You will be comfortable working in a deeply technical environment, working daily with platform and systems engineers, while translating progress, risks and trade-offs into clear reporting senior stakeholders can trust. You will thrive in ambiguity and an organisation where you are able to drive change.&amp;nbsp;You do not just coordinate: you unblock teams, keep plans honest, and raise the bar on how programmes are run.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have prior experience tunning technical programmes across multiple engineering teams, ideally in infrastructure, platform or systems engineering environments. You should be fluent with modern programme tooling, such as Jira, Confluence and GitHub, and have the judgement to keep process lightweight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’d be a great fit with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience harmonising ways of working across sibling teams or departments, integrating processes rather than multiplying them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong, plain-English communication and the ability to make infrastructure work legible to non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple workstreams simultaneously across sites and time zones in a fast-paced, changing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A chase-without-nagging, escalate-without-drama working style, and a clear sense of the difference between a risk and a noise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional experience would be beneficial, such as a background in hardware-adjacent software (labs, manufacturing, robotics, scientific instruments), exposure to regulated or government-customer delivery, or agile coaching / scrum mastery experience. Working knowledge of quantum computing concepts would be a plus though is not essential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be part of a team that’s shaping the future of quantum. We offer more than just a role, you’ll join a world class community of scientists, engineers and innovators working to unlock the full potential of quantum computing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer a range of benefits, including opportunities to further your career alongside industry leaders, a competitive salary with IonQ stock options, an annual performance bonus, generous annual leave, flexible hybrid working, private medical and dental insurance for you and your family, and much more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and be part of the future of quantum computing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer and welcome applicants from all backgrounds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IonQ, we believe in fair treatment, access, opportunity, and advancement for all while striving to identify and eliminate barriers. We empower employees to thrive by fostering a culture of autonomy, productivity, and respect. We are dedicated to creating an environment where individuals can feel welcomed, respected, supported, and valued.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to equity and justice. We welcome different voices and viewpoints and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. We are proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;The position you are applying for will require access to technology that is subject to U.S. export control and government contract restrictions.&amp;nbsp; Employment with IonQ is contingent on either verifying “U.S. Person” (e.g., U.S. citizen, U.S. national, U.S. permanent resident, or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum) status for export controls and government contracts work, obtaining any necessary license, and/or confirming the availability of a license exception under U.S. export controls.&amp;nbsp; Please note that in the absence of confirming you are a U.S. Person for export control and government contracts work purposes, IonQ may choose not to apply for a license or decline to use a license exception (if available) for you to access export-controlled technology that may require authorization, and similarly, you may not qualify for government contracts work that requires U.S. Persons, and IonQ may decline to proceed with your application on those bases alone.&amp;nbsp; Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Non-Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Due to applicable export control laws and regulations, candidates must be a U.S. citizen or national, U.S. permanent resident (i.e., current Green Card holder), or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum. Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in being a part of our team and mission, we encourage you to apply!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Klaviyo, we value the unique backgrounds, experiences and perspectives each Klaviyo (we call ourselves Klaviyos) brings to our workplace each and every day. We believe everyone deserves a fair shot at success and appreciate the experiences each person brings beyond the traditional job requirements. If you’re a close but not exact match with the description, we hope you’ll still consider applying. Want to learn more about life at Klaviyo? Visit &lt;a class=&quot;_ymio1r31 _ypr0glyw _zcxs1o36 _mizu194a _1ah3dkaa _ra3xnqa1 _128mdkaa _1cvmnqa1 _4davt94y _4bfu18uv _1hms8stv _ajmmnqa1 _vchhusvi _kqswh2mm _ect4ttxp _syaz13af _1a3b18uv _4fpr8stv _5goinqa1 _f8pj13af _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _30l313af _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _9h8h12zz _10531ra0 _1ien1ra0 _n0fx1ra0 _1vhv17z1&quot; href=&quot;http://klaviyo.com/careers&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;klaviyo.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to see how we empower creators to own their own destiny.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;London, UK (Hybrid 3 days p/week in office)&lt;br&gt;12 month full-time fixed term contact (starting: 1 Nov 2026)&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Lifecycle Marketing Team at Klaviyo is a Center of Excellence that delivers seamless scalable customer-facing experiences across all owned channels, and servicing all segments and geographies. We own channel performance and optimisation while driving measurable impact at every stage of the customer lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior individual contributor role, and as our Lead Lifecycle Marketer for EMEA within the global Lifecycle Marketing team, you’ll own lifecycle marketing across the region, partnering with EMEA Marketing and Sales to identify opportunities and deliver programs that support regional growth and business priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also partner with the global Lifecycle Marketing team to localise and scale global programs for EMEA, ensuring lifecycle experiences are relevant to local markets, audiences, and customer needs. This is a hands-on execution-focused role combining optimisation, strategy, and cross-functional collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMEA Lifecycle Programs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategy and execution of EMEA-specific lifecycle programs and campaigns in partnership with regional Marketing, Sales and Partner teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support EMEA Events with lifecycle strategy and execution for key regional and flagship Klaviyo events for prospects, customers and partners, from targeting and invitations through to post-event nurture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own audience and segmentation strategies using customer, prospect, firmographic, behavioural, and engagement data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define success metrics, analyse performance across markets and segments, and turn insights into testing and optimisation opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Lifecycle Programs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the global Lifecycle Marketing team to localise and regionalise Sales-Led, PLG, onboarding, adoption, re-engagement, and cross-sell programs for EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide EMEA input into global lifecycle strategy, segmentation, channel optimisation, and testing, using regional insights to improve performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Growth, PMM, Brand, and other global teams to scale relevant lifecycle initiatives across EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional &amp;amp; Operational Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align the EMEA lifecycle roadmap with global and regional stakeholders, balancing global priorities with market needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multiple initiatives, making clear prioritisation and trade-off decisions while maintaining quality and pace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion customer-first initiatives and ensure lifecycle experiences are relevant, scalable, measurable, and operationally sound.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experiences &amp;amp; Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in Lifecycle Marketing, Demand Gen, PLG Marketing, Performance Marketing, CRM, and/or Email Marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B2B and international experience, ideally EMEA within a company with a North American HQ&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of lifecycle/marketing best practices: deliverability, personalisation, segmentation, testing, reporting, channel optimisation, backed by a data-driven approach to audience performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Native/ fluent English (essential). Fluent French/ German/ Spanish/ Italian a bonus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tools &amp;amp; Tech:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with lifecycle and CRM technologies including: HubSpot (essential), Salesforce (essential), Smartling (nice to have) and other localisation and marketing automation platforms advantageous&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monday board or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional/stakeholder&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional operator, able to align stakeholders across regional/ global Marketing, Sales, Growth, Product, Operations teams across different timezones&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work style&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execution and delivery focused: Hands-on across strategy, analysis, managing multiple projects and trade-offs in a fast-paced, shifting environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid 3 days p/ week in the London office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full work authorisation to work in the UK without any restrictions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;#LI-Hybrid #LI-JW1&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Our salary range reflects the cost of labour in the country where the job post is advertised. The base salary offered for this position is determined by several factors, including the applicant’s job-related skills, relevant experience, education or training, and work location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to base salary, our total compensation package may include participation in the company’s annual cash bonus plan, variable compensation (OTE) for sales and customer success roles, equity, sign-on payments, and a comprehensive range of health, welfare, and wellbeing benefits based on eligibility.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your recruiter can provide more details about the specific salary/OTE&amp;nbsp; range for your preferred location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range in Local Currency:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£80,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£120,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role may require up to 10% travel for purposes such as new hire onboarding, client or partner work if applicable, team meetings, and industry events. Travel is coordinated in advance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get to Know Klaviyo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re Klaviyo (pronounced clay-vee-oh). We empower creators to own their destiny by making first-party data accessible and actionable like never before. We see limitless potential for the technology we’re developing to nurture personalized experiences in ecommerce and beyond. To reach our goals, we need our own crew of remarkable creators—ambitious and collaborative teammates who stay focused on our north star: delighting our customers. If you’re ready to do the best work of your career, where you’ll be welcomed as your whole self from day one and supported with generous benefits, we hope you’ll join us.&lt;/p&gt;
