&lt;h1&gt;Sr. Software Engineer&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Team + The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pendo&#39;s engineering teams build the product experiences that help customers understand, improve, and act on product usage data. This team is focused on AI-powered features that turn raw usage signals into automatic, actionable suggestions, reducing the manual work customers need to do before they can get value from Pendo.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Software Engineer, you will help shape and ship intelligent product experiences from discovery through delivery. You will work full-stack with a lean toward frontend, using TypeScript, Vue.js, backend services, and AI coding tools to build high-quality features on a small, fast-moving team. This role also owns product judgment: validating problems with customers, sizing opportunities, defining success metrics, and making pragmatic tradeoffs in ambiguous spaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in our Sheffield office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What this looks like day-to-day&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-powered feature delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and ship features that use AI to turn product usage data into actionable suggestions for customers. You will work end to end across the experience, with attention to quality, usability, and the unique failure modes of AI-backed products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full-stack engineering:&lt;/strong&gt; Own delivery across the frontend and backend, with a strong lean toward TypeScript, Vue.js, DOM-level work, component architecture, and in-browser data capture. You will reason about backend services and APIs while building polished, reliable customer-facing experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product discovery:&lt;/strong&gt; Help validate problems, shape scope, and test direction before and while building. You will join customer calls, test prototypes, and use real feedback to make sure the team is solving meaningful problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Success metrics and iteration:&lt;/strong&gt; Define what success looks like for the features you build and use product usage data to guide iteration. You will not just close tickets; you will measure whether the work is creating the intended customer impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-enabled development:&lt;/strong&gt; Use AI coding tools such as Cursor and Claude Code as a core part of your daily workflow. You will apply strong engineering judgment, review rigor, and accountability to AI-generated code just as you would to your own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI product quality:&lt;/strong&gt; Ship AI-backed features with careful attention to latency, hallucination, inconsistent output, and user trust. You will help ensure intelligent experiences are useful, understandable, and reliable for customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Work directly with product, design, and fellow engineers in a small team where ownership and leverage matter. You will help make pragmatic tradeoffs against ambiguous, fast-moving requirements instead of waiting for a fully defined spec.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering standards:&lt;/strong&gt; Raise the quality of the team through code review, mentorship, and unblocking teammates. You will communicate clearly, share context, and help others grow while keeping delivery moving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who You Are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond the qualifications, we hire through a specific lens. These aren&#39;t buzzwords; they&#39;re the things we&#39;ll actually look for in how you talk about your work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re a builder, not a maintainer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re most energized when there isn&#39;t a clear path yet, and you get to define it. You don&#39;t wait for direction; you identify gaps, shape solutions, and drive them forward. At Pendo, great Senior Software Engineers don&#39;t just follow instructions; they operate as strategic advisors, influencing decisions, guiding stakeholders, and elevating how we work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re AI-curious - genuinely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re not using AI tools occasionally. You&#39;re rewiring how you work around them. You&#39;re faster, sharper, and more prolific because of it, and you bring that energy to everything — how you approach your work, how you prep, how you communicate, how you think. We want someone who sees AI as a multiplier, not a shortcut.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must-haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building with LLMs and AI agents, whether through production work or personal projects. You have built something with these technologies, not just used them as tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full-stack engineering experience with a frontend lean, including strong TypeScript skills, comfort working with the DOM, and the ability to reason about backend services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience building and scaling web applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgment, including comfort owning ambiguous problems, shaping scope, and making decisions without a fully specified brief.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining success metrics for a feature and iterating based on real usage data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging directly with customers or end users to validate problems and assess impact after launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong grasp of software architecture, design principles, and API development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication skills and the ability to mentor others, unblock teammates, and support the growth of the engineering team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice-to-haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working as, or closely alongside, a product manager, including writing specs, prioritizing a roadmap, or running discovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with product analytics tools such as Pendo, Amplitude, or Mixpanel to measure feature impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or running experiments, including A/B tests or betas, to validate product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with browser DOM inspection or automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Model Context Protocol or building tools for LLM agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with real-time data pipelines or streaming architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accessibility experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for continuous learning and sharing insights with the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Pendo&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pendo was founded in 2013 by former product managers, who combined their heads and hearts to build something they wanted but never had as product managers: a simple way to understand and attack what truly drives product success. Our mission is to improve society&#39;s experience with software. Come join one of the fastest-growing startups, supported by best-in-class institutions like Battery Ventures, Salesforce Ventures, Spark Capital and Meritech.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pendo Core Values:&lt;/strong&gt; Bias to Act, Hone Your Craft, The Team is Pendo, and Maniacal Focus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Pendo is a hybrid culture. In-office 3 days per week unless designated remote.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt; The expected salary range for this role to be performed in Sheffield, United Kingdom is £60,000 - £78,000.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt; Comprehensive, top-tier coverage in the United Kingdom, including medical, dental, and life coverage, combined with pension match, equity, and high-value lifestyle perks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEOC:&lt;/strong&gt; We are an equal opportunity employer and believe having diverse teams where everyone brings their whole self to Pendo is key to our success. We welcome all people of different backgrounds, experiences, abilities and perspectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accessibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Pendo is committed to working with, and providing access and reasonable accommodation to, applicants with mental and/or physical disabilities. If you think you may require an accommodation for any part of the recruitment process, please send a request to: ----- All requests for accommodations are treated discreetly and confidentially, as practical and permitted by law.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;The Team + The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pendo’s &lt;strong&gt;Customer Engineering team&lt;/strong&gt; is the technical backbone of the&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;pre- and post-sales customer motion.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team brings together work across Customer Success, Technical Account Management, and Solutions Engineering into one full-lifecycle technical owner. Customer Engineering helps customers connect technical execution to business outcomes and realize the value of their investment in Pendo.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Customer Engineer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;you will own strategic and complex Enterprise accounts across acquisition, implementation, adoption, expansion, and escalation. You will lead technical strategy for complex deployments, resolve ambiguous customer challenges, and partner closely with account teams to drive retention, expansion, and customer value. Your impact will extend beyond your own accounts through playbooks, coaching, repeatable fixes, and workflow improvements that raise the capability of the broader Customer Engineering team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in our&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;London office.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What this looks like day-to-day&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;New customer acquisition and selling:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Partner with Account Directors on&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;pre-sales&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;motions for&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;new customer acquisition, product expansion, and growth across lines of business.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;You identify customer pain, craft and deliver tailored demos, and lead technical evaluations through requirements gathering, success criteria, installation guidance, and hands-on workshops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quarterly business outcomes:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Drive measurable improvement in customer health, retention, expansion, and technical resolution across strategic accounts. You contribute at least one reusable framework, playbook, or process that other Customer Engineers use and become a trusted advisor to Account Directors on account health and technical strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adoption, expansion, and growth:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Identify opportunities to&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;expand adoption&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;across underutilized features, untapped products, and new lines of business. When adoption stalls, you diagnose root causes, design a path forward, and connect technical work to measurable business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complex implementations and value realization:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Lead onboarding for strategic customers, including planning, implementation, integrations, and training. You build customer-specific implementation playbooks, guide complex deployments with executive visibility, and ensure customers realize value during onboarding and over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team capability building:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Build playbooks, document repeatable fixes, coach peers, and improve how Customer Engineering work gets done across the team. You use AI tools to accelerate content creation, surface patterns across accounts, and share practical workflow findings with the broader team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Early account impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Assess account health, risks, stakeholder relationships, and the highest-priority problems to solve within your portfolio. You establish trust with Account Directors and customer stakeholders, then independently lead complex customer interactions that move accounts forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical escalation:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Serve as an escalation point for complex technical challenges raised by other Customer Engineers. You resolve ambiguous problems with multiple variables and tradeoffs, involving Product or Engineering only when truly needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who You Are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond the qualifications, we hire through a specific lens. These aren&#39;t buzzwords; they&#39;re the things we&#39;ll actually look for in how you talk about your work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re a builder, not a maintainer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;You&#39;re most energized when there isn&#39;t a clear path yet, and you get to define it. You don&#39;t wait for direction; you identify gaps, shape solutions, and drive them forward. At Pendo, great Senior Customer Engineers don&#39;t just follow instructions; they operate as strategic advisors, influencing decisions, guiding stakeholders, and elevating how we work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re AI-curious - genuinely.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;You&#39;re not using AI tools occasionally. You&#39;re rewiring how you work around them. You&#39;re faster, sharper, and more prolific because of it, and you bring that energy to everything — how you approach your work, how you prep, how you communicate, how you think. We want someone who sees AI as a multiplier, not a shortcut.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must-haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for working with customers and building strong and impactful customer relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 to 8 years of experience in a customer-facing technical role such as Solutions Engineering, Technical Account Management, Customer Engineering, implementation, professional services, or solutions architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on experience with web technologies including HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and REST APIs, with the ability to architect and troubleshoot complex front-end implementations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience managing strategic Enterprise accounts with executive-level stakeholders, competing priorities, and complex technical or business requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to solve ambiguous problems involving multiple variables, constraints, and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience connecting technical execution to business outcomes such as retention, expansion, ROI, and value realization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on use of AI tools for account research, content creation, or workflow automation, with demonstrated integration into day-to-day work rather than light experimentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring or coaching more junior technical team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice-to-haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Pendo, digital adoption platforms, product analytics, or in-app experience tooling in an enterprise environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with mobile app development, including Swift, Android, or React Native.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with data architecture, AI or machine learning concepts, or advanced analytics instrumentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of building reusable frameworks, playbooks, or processes that were adopted by a broader team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Pendo&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pendo was founded in 2013 by former product managers, who combined their heads and hearts to build something they wanted but never had as product managers: a simple way to understand and attack what truly drives product success. Our mission is to improve society&#39;s experience with software. Come join one of the fastest-growing startups, supported by best-in-class institutions like Battery Ventures, Salesforce Ventures, Spark Capital and Meritech.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pendo Core Values:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Bias to Act, Hone Your Craft, The Team is Pendo, and Maniacal Focus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Pendo is a hybrid culture. In-office 3 days per week in London, UK&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of many compensation, benefits and other reward opportunities we provide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt; Comprehensive, top-tier coverage (medical, dental, life) combined with pension match, equity, and high-value lifestyle perks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEOC:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We are an equal opportunity employer and believe having diverse teams where everyone brings their whole self to Pendo is key to our success. We welcome all people of different backgrounds, experiences, abilities and perspectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accessibility:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Pendo is committed to working with, and providing access and reasonable accommodation to, applicants with mental and/or physical disabilities. If you think you may require an accommodation for any part of the recruitment process, please send a request to: ----- All requests for accommodations are treated discreetly and confidentially, as practical and permitted by law.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Marketing Director&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to: Chief Commercial Officer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;UK, France, Netherlands, Belgium, Germany, Austria, Spain, Finland, USA. Some travel to our offices will be required from time-to-time&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You must have the right to work in one the above countries in order to be considered for the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💼 About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PQShield is looking for a Product Marketing Director who can turn complex technology into stories that people understand, remember, and act on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own how PQShield&#39;s products, technology, and vision are positioned, communicated, and brought to market worldwide. You&#39;ll sit at the intersection of product, engineering, sales, customers, and the broader security market — translating breakthrough cryptography and security technology into compelling narratives for executives, engineers, partners, and buyers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is for a strategic product marketer and exceptional storyteller who can identify the market shift, understand the customer problem, and turn complex technology into differentiated positioning that creates urgency, preference and demand.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since NIST published its first post-quantum cryptography (PQC) standards, which the PQShield team co-authored, organizations across semiconductors, automotive, defense, and enterprise face significant challenges in preparing for the post-quantum transition. This role will help define the market narrative around that transition, position PQShield&#39;s portfolio within it and give customers a clear reason to act.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;⚒️ What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the story: Develop the narrative, positioning, messaging, and value propositions that explain what is changing in the market, why customers need to act, the problem PQShield solves, and why our approach is differentiated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn technical capability into customer value: Work with cryptographers, engineers and product leaders to understand sophisticated technology, identify what matters to the buyer and translate technical capabilities into clear business and security value without sacrificing technical credibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position the portfolio: Own positioning and messaging for our hardware IP and software portfolio, including PQPlatform, PQPerform, PQCryptoLib, and PQMicroLib. Build a clear messaging architecture that connects the portfolio while preserving the differentiated value of each offering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the customer: Develop deep insight into customer problems, buying journeys, security requirements, regulatory pressures, barriers to adoption, buying dynamics, and the forces driving post-quantum adoption. Turn those insights into sharper products, messaging, and go-to-market strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape category and market narrative: Help define how PQShield talks about post-quantum security, cryptographic agility, and the transition to quantum-safe systems — and how we differentiate our approach in a rapidly evolving market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead product launches: Create and execute compelling go-to-market strategies for new products, certifications, partnerships, and major releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equip the sales team: Build compelling presentations, stories, solution briefs, case studies, battlecards, and other tools that help sales teams communicate value and win complex deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build buyer and segment-specific stories: Develop differentiated narratives for semiconductors, automotive, military and aerospace, industrial IoT, networking, and enterprise, adapting the value story for different buyers, use cases and business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own competitive storytelling: Understand the competitive landscape and turn technical and commercial differences into clear, credible differentiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create exceptional content: Lead the development of white papers, thought leadership, application notes, customer stories, executive content, web experiences, and other material that establishes PQShield as a category leader.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring customer stories to life: Find and develop the stories that demonstrate why customers are making the transition to post-quantum security and why they choose PQShield.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across the company: Partner closely with product, engineering, sales, partnerships, and leadership to ensure the market sees one clear, compelling PQShield story.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎯 Required Skills And Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an experienced product marketing leader who is exceptionally strong in positioning, messaging and strategic storytelling. You can take an emerging market, complicated buyer problem or deeply technical product and find the clear narrative inside it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of marketing experience, with significant experience in product marketing, technology marketing, B2B marketing, or a closely related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to develop positioning and stories that change how markets understand a product, technology, or company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills. You can take something highly technical and make it understandable, interesting, and compelling without dumbing it down.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong storytelling instincts and the ability to find the human, business, and strategic narrative inside complex technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing technical B2B products, ideally in cybersecurity, semiconductors, infrastructure, embedded systems, software, or another sophisticated technology market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of security and technology buyers, and the ability to communicate credibly with CISOs, CTOs, engineers, architects, product leaders, and business executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work closely with technical experts and quickly develop enough subject-matter expertise to challenge assumptions, ask good questions, and tell an accurate story.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong commercial mindset: you understand that great marketing isn&#39;t just about explaining a product — it&#39;s about creating differentiation, urgency, preference, and ultimately revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching products and taking complex offerings to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing compelling sales narratives and enablement for complex, multi-stakeholder sales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent strategic judgment, with the ability to determine what the market needs to hear, why it matters, and how PQShield should say it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in a fast-moving environment where you will often need to create the narrative before the market has established one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we can offer you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A competitive compensation package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A remote first company. You will work from home most of the time, but will need to join us in the office for planning sessions and key meetings as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel for customer meetings and marketing events as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health insurance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO and holiday package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company contributions towards 401K/pension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;…and other great benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you enjoy working as part of a technology company, value the security of our daily digital lives, and love solving hard problems - then we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PQShield is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. We’re passionate about talent and proud to foster an inclusive environment; all applicants will be considered regardless of their gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability, and age.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;PQShield is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. We’re passionate about talent and proud to foster an inclusive environment; all applicants will be considered regardless of their gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability, and age.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Pinterest:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Millions of people around the world come to our platform to find creative ideas, dream about new possibilities and plan for memories that will last a lifetime. At Pinterest, we’re on a mission to bring everyone the inspiration to create a life they love, and that starts with the people behind the product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Discover a career where you ignite innovation for millions, transform passion into growth opportunities, celebrate each other’s unique experiences and embrace the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinterestcareers.com/our-life/pinflex/&quot;&gt;flexibility&lt;/a&gt; to do your best work. Creating a career you love? It’s Possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Pinterest, AI isn&#39;t just a feature, it&#39;s a powerful partner that augments our creativity and amplifies our impact, and we’re looking for candidates who are excited to be a part of that. To get a complete picture of your experience and abilities, we’ll explore your foundational skills and how you collaborate with AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through our interview process, what matters most is that you can always explain your approach, showing us not just what you know, but how you think. You can read more about our AI interview philosophy and how we use AI in our recruiting process &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinterestcareers.com/our-philosophy-on-ai-in-hiring/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pinterest is looking for a Lead Global Client Partner to drive growth across our largest multinational advertiser partnerships. You’ll lead global commercial strategy, senior client relationships and cross-market growth initiatives, helping shape how Pinterest partners with global advertisers at scale. This role sits on the Global Accounts team and is focused on revenue acceleration, enterprise influence and multi-market execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead global commercial strategy for assigned enterprise partnerships, including JBPs, global negotiations and cross-market growth initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain senior relationships with global client and agency stakeholders, positioning Pinterest as a strategic business partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and unlock new budgets, brands, categories and geographic growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align regional teams around global priorities and translate strategy into coordinated market execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage in frequent in-person client meetings and international travel to build relationships, drive alignment and unlock growth across markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create scalable frameworks that reduce duplication, remove friction and increase speed across markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clear visibility into pipeline, risks and opportunities across assigned partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI to accelerate analysis, planning and preparation, applying judgment and verification to ensure accuracy and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build AI-enabled workflows to automate repeatable tasks, synthesize information and improve productivity in a high-volume environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading large, complex global or multi-market advertiser relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving commercial growth through enterprise partnerships, strategic agreements or cross-market initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with senior client, agency and internal stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness and ability to travel frequently, including international travel, to support senior client relationships and multi-market collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of digital advertising, media, technology or adjacent industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in ambiguous, fast-changing environments with multiple priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong prioritization skills, including making clear trade-offs in resource-constrained environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to use AI to improve speed and quality in day-to-day work, with clear judgment, verification and ownership of final outputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field such as Business, Marketing or Communications, or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relocation Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position is not eligible for relocation assistance. Visit our&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinterestcareers.com/pinflex/&quot;&gt; PinFlex&lt;/a&gt; page to learn more about our working model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Office Requirement Statement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We recognize that the ideal environment for work is situational and may differ across departments. What this looks like day-to-day can vary based on the needs of each organization or role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role will need to be in the office for in-person collaboration 3 times per week and therefore needs to be in a commutable distance from our Paris or London office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role also includes frequent international travel and regular in-person client engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-HYBRID&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#SL2&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Pinterest we believe the workplace should be equitable, inclusive, and inspiring for every employee. In an effort to provide greater transparency, we are sharing the base salary range for this position. The position is also eligible for equity and incentive compensation. Final salary is based on a number of factors including location, travel, relevant prior experience, or particular skills and expertise.&lt;/p&gt;
